  "note": "First election of the county council under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1898; polled 6 April 1899 and counted the next day at the County Courthouse, Armagh, before J. G. Sharkey, sub-sheriff. Two candidates named T. Knipe (of different townlands) stood; the Lurgan Mail lists only the first. The second, with 3 votes, is from the Northern Star."
